From: sss@dark-alexandr.net
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 04:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ik-llama-kimi-k3: add missing KV name mappings

Two KV keys (LLM_KV_EXPERT_LATENT_LENGTH and LLM_KV_ATTN_RES_BLOCK_SIZE)
were added to the enum in llama-arch.h but not to the LLM_KV_NAMES
mapping table in llama-arch.cpp.  When llm_kv::operator() calls
LLM_KV_NAMES.at(kv) for either, std::out_of_range ("map::at") is thrown.

diff --git a/src/llama-arch.cpp b/src/llama-arch.cpp
index c17e15c3..29343916 100644
--- a/src/llama-arch.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-arch.cpp
@@ -168,6 +168,7 @@ static const std::map<llm_kv, const char *> LLM_KV_NAMES = {
     { LLM_KV_EXPERT_WEIGHTS_NORM,               "%s.expert_weights_norm"               },
     { LLM_KV_EXPERT_GATING_FUNC,                "%s.expert_gating_func"                },
+    { LLM_KV_EXPERT_LATENT_LENGTH,              "%s.expert_latent_length"              },
     // K2 Horizon MoVA
     { LLM_KV_ATTENTION_GROUPNORM_GROUPS,       "%s.attention.group_norm_groups"        },
     { LLM_KV_ATTENTION_VALUE_EXPERT_COUNT,     "%s.attention.value_expert_count"       },
@@ -174,6 +175,7 @@ static const std::map<llm_kv, const char *> LLM_KV_NAMES = {
 
     { LLM_KV_NEXTN_PREDICT_LAYERS,              "%s.nextn_predict_layers"              },
+    { LLM_KV_ATTN_RES_BLOCK_SIZE,               "%s.attn_res.block_size"               },
     { LLM_KV_NUM_DEEPSTACK_LAYERS,              "%s.n_deepstack_layers"                },
     { LLM_KV_POOLING_TYPE,                      "%s.pooling_type"                      },
